The method offer adds element e (non-null). The comment: "If the element is not null, then the element at the head of the queue after adding is less than or equal to the element that was at the head before adding."

We need to express: if e != null then after the operation, the head element (i.e., peek()) is <= old head element (i.e., \old(this.peek())) according to ordering.

But ordering may be natural or comparator. Need to use comparator if present, else comparable.

